# Fallback Model Allowlist

Adding a fallback table row requires naming 004's recommendation, the fallback vendor's Article 21 assessment, and the failover rows of the zero-retention and transfer-basis documents, with the `evidence` string copied from the fallback assessment's Allowlist row. ([validated by names #7, #28, #29 and #30 in the evidence of every non-mock entry](../../apps/api/test/models.test.ts#L57))

Any future `HalEngineConfig` field carrying a `ProviderConfig` extends the resolver's input type. ([validated by the resolver accepts every ProviderConfig in the assembled config](../../apps/api/test/fallback-model.acceptance.test.ts#L59))

The `api.model` startup log line includes a `fallback` block with `providerType`, `model`, and `region` when a fallback model is configured; a nested object whose string values are not on the logger-safe key allowlist is dropped rather than logged. ([validated by `keeps a nested object whose string values are all under safe keys`](../../apps/api/test/logger.test.ts#L71), [validated by `api.model line gains the fallback block`](../../apps/api/test/fallback-model-log.acceptance.test.ts#L32))

The provider block hands HAL Engine the resolved fallback as the only entry of `fallbackProviders`, the one setting HAL Engine fails over through, and an empty list while `FALLBACK_MODEL_ID` is unset, so the fallback the `api.model` line names is the one HAL Engine tries when the primary is unavailable. (#474) ([validated by `hands HAL Engine the mock and an empty fallbackProviders list when FALLBACK_MODEL_ID is unset`](../../apps/api/test/server.test.ts#L171), [validated by `hands HAL Engine the mock fallback as the only fallbackProviders entry when FALLBACK_MODEL_ID is mock`](../../apps/api/test/server.test.ts#L178))

Only the mock row can be a fallback until a fallback vendor is chosen (KU-07): building a real fallback needs that vendor's own settings, so a `FALLBACK_MODEL_ID` naming any other row is refused at startup with a message naming `FALLBACK_MODEL_ID`, the id, its provider type and KU-07. (#474) ([validated by `refuses FALLBACK_MODEL_ID gemini-3.1-flash-lite before any config is built, naming its vertex row and KU-07`](../../apps/api/test/fallback-model.acceptance.test.ts#L70))

The mock is refused at startup as the fallback of a `MODEL_ID` that is not the mock: it echoes each customer's own message back as the answer, so behind a real model it would turn that model's outage into answers that pass for success, where the agent must hand off. (#474) ([validated by `refuses the mock as the fallback of MODEL_ID gemini-3.1-flash-lite before any config is built, since it would echo each customer back`](../../apps/api/test/fallback-model.acceptance.test.ts#L78))


